@startuml preferences
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Preferences: Local Edit Capture, Per-Field Merge and Echo Suppression

participant "SyncService" as Service
participant "PreferencesSync" as Pref
participant "SettingsManager" as Settings
participant "SyncRevisionClock" as Clock
database "Local UserDefaults\nsync.preferences / sync.counter" as Local
participant "SyncRepository" as Repo

Service -> Pref : synchronize(reading: refreshRequested)
Pref -> Clock : observe local field revisions
Pref -> Settings : current syncPreferences
Pref -> Pref : compare with lastObservedValues\nnew revisions only for fields changed locally
Pref -> Clock : nextRevision (when there are edits)
Pref -> Local : save only if local content changed; commit counter
note over Pref,Local : local intent is saved before waiting on cloud I/O

opt explicit refresh or needsInitialRead
  Pref -> Repo : read(.preferences)
  Repo --> Pref : device records + conflict versions
  Pref -> Pref : check cancellation
  Pref -> Clock : observe the highest record and field counters
  Pref -> Settings : current settings again
  Pref -> Pref : capture local edits made during I/O again\nallocate revisions after the observed remote counters
  Pref -> Pref : mergedPreferences.merge(incoming)\ncompare SyncRevision per field
  Pref -> Settings : validate known fields as a whole, then apply changes
  Pref -> Pref : update mergedPreferences\nlastObservedValues = settings actually applied\nrestore this device's published baseline; needsInitialRead = false
  note over Pref,Settings
    Applying remote values may fire the settings subscription,
    but with the baseline updated, the next round does not treat it as a local edit.
  end note
end

Pref -> Pref : fill in local values only for fields missing from the merge\nnew-device defaults never overwrite existing remote fields
Pref -> Local : save the local merged copy only on change; commit counter
alt mergedPreferences != lastPublishedPreferences
  Pref -> Clock : makeRecord (increment and persist counter)
  Pref -> Repo : write(.preferences)
  Repo --> Pref : success
  Pref -> Pref : after checking cancellation, update lastPublishedPreferences
else nothing new
  note over Pref,Repo : publication skipped
end

note over Pref,Local
  mergedPreferences: the domain's truth (values + revisions)
  lastObservedValues: baseline for recognizing local edits
  persistedPreferences: local persistence baseline
  lastPublishedPreferences: this connection's publication baseline

  Disconnecting resets only the publication baseline and first-read flag;
  the local copy for restoring edits is kept.
end note
@enduml
